 # Aligned halfword RAM packing
 
+Integration note: production keeps `NETBOOT_STORE16_PACKING=0` by default,
+which uses the newer `netboot_copy` aligned-word implementation. Set
+`NETBOOT_STORE16_PACKING=1` to select the historical aligned-halfword candidate.
+Both implementations retain immutable, non-overlapping RX source ownership,
+aligned destination stores, exact byte bounds, range checks and return codes.
+The independent native oracle below now covers both production modes. Historical
+CPU results below apply only to the original matched experiment, not this merge.
+
 This third isolated optimization preserves the qualified sum16 and CRC changes. After the original prefix aligns destination RAM, an even source uses four aligned GCC may_alias halfword loads per8bytes and the existing aligned volatile64-bit RAM store. Odd sources retain byte packing. Prefix, tail, image-range checks and return codes remain unchanged. The target is explicitly little-endian; no overlapping-copy contract is added.
 
-Run `python3 scripts/test_netboot_store16.py --out build/netboot-store16-native`. Existing GCC-compatible tools with ASan/UBSan are required; `--cc` selects one and `--dry-run` only checks source identity/prints scope. The runner compares exact production and extracted candidate bodies and reconstructs original board sourceSHA `b4197681463b8ff4277f0c45f2bcec9f4bfd0b134dbc4d78f6f260ba83e1b59c`. Tests cover393,408 independent byte comparisons across8×8source/destination alignments,lengths0..2048,3patterns;20range cases includingUINT32_MAX and unchanged memory after rejection;130real protected guard-page boundaries. Whole destination sentinels and an exact intentional-corruption negative are required. LSan is disabled; ASan/UBSan remain active. Guard pages complement source bounds proof and ASan poison-granularity limits.
+Run `python3 scripts/test_netboot_store16.py --out build/netboot-store16-native`. Existing GCC-compatible tools with ASan/UBSan are required; `--cc` selects one and `--dry-run` only checks source identity/prints scope. The runner compares exact production and extracted candidate bodies for both selector modes. The runner pins the unchanged independent original store fixture SHA rather than the historical whole-board SHA, because current board clock and transport changes must be retained. For each mode, tests cover393,408 independent byte comparisons across8×8source/destination alignments,lengths0..2048,3patterns;20range cases includingUINT32_MAX and unchanged memory after rejection;130real protected guard-page boundaries. Whole destination sentinels and an exact intentional-corruption negative are required. LSan is disabled; ASan/UBSan remain active. Guard pages complement source bounds proof and ASan poison-granularity limits.
 
